# InsightFlow.Web conventions

- Blazor Web App, Interactive Server. Pages in `Components/Pages`, feature components in `Components/Workspace`
  (or a new feature folder), primitives in `Components/Ui` (Button, Pane, DataTable, Alert, Spinner, EmptyState, Icon).
- Styling: Tailwind v4 utility classes only. Use the tokens in `Styles/app.css` (`brand-*`, slate neutrals,
  `dark:` variants) and shared class strings in `UiStyles`. No inline `<style>`, no component libraries without Roy's OK.
- Call services only through the typed clients in `Services/` (`WorkspaceApiClient`, `QueryApiClient`, `AgentApiClient`).
  Catch `ServiceCallException` and show `<Alert Message="..." />`. Never use a raw `HttpClient` in components.
- Large files go through the BFF endpoints (`/bff/workspace/...`), never over the SignalR circuit. State-changing
  BFF calls must send the `X-InsightFlow-Request` header.
- Charts: build a `VizSpec`, call `QueryApiClient.VizAsync`, render with `<VizRenderer Spec Result />`. Extend
  `Charts/VegaLiteSpecBuilder.cs` for new encodings, with a golden test in `tests/InsightFlow.Web.Tests`.
- JS interop: ES modules in `wwwroot/js/`, imported with `JS.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./js/x.js")`.
  Dispose modules and `DotNetObjectReference`s (`IAsyncDisposable`) and catch `JSDisconnectedException` on dispose.
- Front-end packages: pin exact versions in `package.json` (+ `package-lock.json`), vendored by the MSBuild step.
  Never load scripts from a CDN.
- Re-render gotcha: a handler declared in a child component re-renders only that child. Parent state changes need
  `StateHasChanged()` in the parent's method (see `ExplorerPane`).
- Accessibility: buttons are `<button type="button">`, inputs have labels/`aria-label`, and trees/lists use roles.
